ure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135865598,imgsize-161940.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Govt healthcare spend up 3x since 2013-14 to 4.1L cr]]></title><description><![CDATA[Out-Of-Pocket Expense Dips But Families Still Paid 4L Cr In 2023-24]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-healthcare-spend-up-3x-since-2013-14-to-4-1l-cr/articleshow/135865380.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-healthcare-spend-up-3x-since-2013-14-to-4-1l-cr/articleshow/135865380.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T02:04:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135865413,imgsize-58866.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Congress suggests Army ‘friendly fire’ behind deaths of 2 SPOs, BJP calls it 'provocative']]></title><description><![CDATA[In Jammu and Kashmir, Congress has called for a thorough investigation into the tragic killing of two special police officers. Initial reports indicate that the officers may have been accidentally shot by Army personnel during a hunting operation. The BJP has dismissed these allegations, claiming they tarnish the integrity of the security forces.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-suggests-army-friendly-fire-behind-deaths-of-2-spos-bjp-calls-it-provocative/articleshow/135864396.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-suggests-army-friendly-fire-behind-deaths-of-2-spos-bjp-calls-it-provocative/articleshow/135864396.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T00:23:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135864500,imgsize-3640810.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mumbai physics forum hosts online lecture by Pak N-scientist]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-physics-forum-hosts-online-lecture-by-pak-n-scientist/articleshow/135863718.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135863718.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Mumbai recently held an online event to honor the birth centenary of Nobel laureate Abdus Salam. Eminent scientist Pervez Amirali Hoodbhoy delivered a lecture discussing Salam's contributions to physics and his life. Hoodbhoy highlighted Salam's significance as a symbol of goodwill between India and Pakistan. He mentioned Salam's lack of recognition in Pakistan due to his Ahmadiyya sect affiliation, affecting youth role models.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-physics-forum-hosts-online-lecture-by-pak-n-scientist/articleshow/135863718.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/mumbai-physics-forum-hosts-online-lecture-by-pak-n-scientist/articleshow/135863718.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T00:14:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Srinivas Laxman</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135863829,imgsize-41814.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kashmir film fraternity trains guns on Bollywood’s ‘AK-47 &amp; skullcap’ stereotype, seeks own industry]]></title><description><![CDATA[Kashmiri filmmakers are advocating for a shift towards regional cinema to enhance authentic storytelling and representation. They argue that Bollywood often reinforces stereotypes that misrepresent life in J&amp;K. The current film policy is criticized for not adequately supporting local productions while favoring external filmmakers. Actors and directors are calling for collaboration among regional artists to develop a unique Kashmiri film industry, signaling a significant movement towards self-identity and cultural expression.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kashmir-film-fraternity-trains-guns-on-bollywoods-ak-47-skullcap-stereotype-seeks-own-industry/articleshow/135863847.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kashmir-film-fraternity-trains-guns-on-bollywoods-ak-47-skullcap-stereotype-seeks-own-industry/articleshow/135863847.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T00:11:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Naseer Ganai</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135864135,imgsize-139986.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kishtwar BJP leader questions Shagun Parihar’s mosque claim, Muslim body seeks public apology]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-bjp-leader-questions-shagun-parihars-mosque-claim-muslim-body-seeks-public-apology/articleshow/135860768.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135860768.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-bjp-leader-questions-shagun-parihars-mosque-claim-muslim-body-seeks-public-apology/articleshow/135860768.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-bjp-leader-questions-shagun-parihars-mosque-claim-muslim-body-seeks-public-apology/articleshow/135860768.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T23:36:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135863278,imgsize-31308.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Launching new anti-anaemia strategy without enough evidence could waste public funds, warn experts]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/launching-new-anti-anaemia-strategy-without-enough-evidence-could-waste-public-funds-warn-experts/articleshow/135862618.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/launching-new-anti-anaemia-strategy-without-enough-evidence-could-waste-public-funds-warn-experts/articleshow/135862618.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T23:18:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rema Nagarajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135862691,imgsize-226640.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Punjab BJP forms manifesto, 'chargesheet' committees; Raghav Chadha, Harbhajan Singh among members]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/punjab-bjp-forms-manifesto-chargesheet-committees-raghav-chadha-harbhajan-singh-among-members/articleshow/135862050.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135862050.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Punjab BJP president Kewal Singh Dhillon has created two vital committees. One will meticulously draft the party manifesto, while the other focuses on compiling a detailed chargesheet. Senior leaders Avinash Rai Khanna and Sunil Jakhar are at the helm, supported by a diverse range of experts, showcasing the party's commitment to thorough preparation for a strategic electoral campaign.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/punjab-bjp-forms-manifesto-chargesheet-committees-raghav-chadha-harbhajan-singh-among-members/articleshow/135862050.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/punjab-bjp-forms-manifesto-chargesheet-committees-raghav-chadha-harbhajan-singh-among-members/articleshow/135862050.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T23:03:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135862175,imgsize-50178.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Well-planned conspiracy': BJP refutes reports of 209-candidate list for upcoming UP elections]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/well-planned-conspiracy-bjp-refutes-reports-of-209-candidate-list-for-upcoming-up-elections/articleshow/135860630.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135860630.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Bharatiya Janata Party's Uttar Pradesh unit has refuted claims regarding a supposed list of 209 candidates. Officials described these reports as false and part of a larger scheme. They cautioned party members against believing in unverified media stories. Additionally, they clarified that the assembly election candidate selection process has yet to commence, highlighting the importance of a methodical and unified approach to such decisions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/well-planned-conspiracy-bjp-refutes-reports-of-209-candidate-list-for-upcoming-up-elections/articleshow/135860630.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/well-planned-conspiracy-bjp-refutes-reports-of-209-candidate-list-for-upcoming-up-elections/articleshow/135860630.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T22:29:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135861024,imgsize-63162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Divide-and-rule tactics': RSS chief Bhagwat's warning over attempts to split India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/divide-and-rule-tactics-rss-chief-bhagwats-warning-over-attempts-to-split-india/articleshow/135856327.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135856327.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[During a recent event in Jodhpur, RSS leader Mohan Bhagwat spoke fervently about the necessity of national unity. He indicated that smaller identities can lead to societal rifts, reminiscent of colonial tactics. Emphasizing the need for individuals to set aside ego and self-interest, he illustrated his points with lessons from the Mahabharata, stressing that unity is key to overcoming challenges.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/divide-and-rule-tactics-rss-chief-bhagwats-warning-over-attempts-to-split-india/articleshow/135856327.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/divide-and-rule-tactics-rss-chief-bhagwats-warning-over-attempts-to-split-india/articleshow/135856327.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T22:19:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135860812,imgsize-113254.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kishtwar SPOs killings: BJP says Congress remarks could fuel Pakistan propaganda, seeks apology]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-spos-killings-bjp-says-congress-remarks-could-fuel-pakistan-propaganda-seeks-apology/articleshow/135860150.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135860150.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-spos-killings-bjp-says-congress-remarks-could-fuel-pakistan-propaganda-seeks-apology/articleshow/135860150.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/kishtwar-spos-killings-bjp-says-congress-remarks-could-fuel-pakistan-propaganda-seeks-apology/articleshow/135860150.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T21:59:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135860365,imgsize-56518.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Won't disappoint my workers': Kumaraswamy says he will decide on Karnataka return at right time]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-disappoint-my-workers-kumaraswamy-says-he-will-decide-on-karnataka-return-at-right-time/articleshow/135860171.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135860171.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-disappoint-my-workers-kumaraswamy-says-he-will-decide-on-karnataka-return-at-right-time/articleshow/135860171.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/wont-disappoint-my-workers-kumaraswamy-says-he-will-decide-on-karnataka-return-at-right-time/articleshow/135860171.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T21:54:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135860212,imgsize-112620.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arunachal governor reviews security in 3 districts, pushes for faster Myanmar border fencing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arunachal-governor-reviews-security-in-3-districts-pushes-for-faster-myanmar-border-fencing/articleshow/135859605.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135859605.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Governor KT Parnaik held a review meeting to assess the security dynamics in Tirap, Changlang, and Longding districts. He emphasized the urgency of advancing the border fencing initiative along the Myanmar border and called for decisive steps against drug trafficking. Highlighting the importance of collaboration among security forces and local administration, the governor voiced his worries over the delays in the fencing project and the increasing drug-related cross-border issues.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arunachal-governor-reviews-security-in-3-districts-pushes-for-faster-myanmar-border-fencing/articleshow/135859605.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arunachal-governor-reviews-security-in-3-districts-pushes-for-faster-myanmar-border-fencing/articleshow/135859605.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T21:39:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135859839,imgsize-51840.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No place for goons': CM Adhikari's warning to criminals after encounter of Shantiniketan accused]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-place-for-goons-cm-adhikaris-warning-to-criminals-after-encounter-of-shantiniketan-accused/articleshow/135859188.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135859188.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a bold statement, Suvendu Adhikari, the Chief Minister of West Bengal, sent a clear message to those involved in crime after a police encounter resulted in the death of Ratan Sheikh, a prime suspect who reportedly shot at officers during his attempted arrest. Adhikari reaffirmed that criminal activities will not be tolerated in the state. Meanwhile, the police constable injured in the incident remains in stable condition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-place-for-goons-cm-adhikaris-warning-to-criminals-after-encounter-of-shantiniketan-accused/articleshow/135859188.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA